# What never leaves this machine (DECISIONS V139, docs/PUBLISHING.md).
#
# tools/publish.sh takes these out of every export (git archive of the
# commit), and tools/pubscan.py refuses an export that still has one, or a
# secret, or a home folder written out. One line a glob:
#   <repo> <glob>     repo: an organisation repository's name, or * for all;
#                     glob: a path from the repository's top (fnmatch; a
#                     name without "/" matches in any folder; "dir/" a folder)
#
# --- every repository: the working notes of the sessions that built it
*  DECISIONS.md
*  CLAUDE.md
*  MEMORY.md
*  .claude/
*  .mcp.json
*  *.memory.md
*  __pycache__/
*  *.pyc
*  .env
*  *.pem
#
# --- veranda (this tree)
# the decisions log: the user's requests quoted, the sessions' notes
veranda  docs/DECISIONS.md
#
# --- mod-player (x16-mod): its working notes and the brief it was built from
mod-player  PLAN.md
mod-player  docs/decisions.md
mod-player  docs/original-brief.md
# (this machine's paths and set-up, written for the sessions)
mod-player  docs/environment.md
#
# --- commander-calc: memory dumps from debugging sessions (untracked today;
#     listed so that they never go in)
commander-calc  dump*.bin
#
# --- geochess: a Windows build of VICE's c1541 (GPL; no source with it):
#     the upstream repository carries it, an export does not
geochess  c1541.exe
